{"tool_name":"anglerfish","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"anglerfish","home":"http://anglerfish.cryst.bbk.ac.uk/","summary":"Method of determining the orientation of an \u03b1-helix relative to a defined axis in a rotationally symmetric protein structure such as a membrane protein channel.","addition_date":"2018-05-19T16:47:41Z","last_update_date":"2019-01-13T18:26:29Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:anglerfish","credit":[{"email":"b.wallace@mail.cryst.bbk.ac.uk","name":"B. Wallace","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-9649-5092","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://anglerfish.cryst.bbk.ac.uk/help.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Protein property calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0250"},{"term":"Protein structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0474"}]}],"name":"AnglerFish","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"migle_sur","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/BIOINFORMATICS/BTW781","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2017 The Author. Published by Oxford University Press.Summary: Integral membrane proteins that form helical pores and bundles constitute major drug targets, and many of their structures have been defined by crystallography and cryo-electron microscopy. The gating of channels and ligand binding of transporters generally involve changes in orientation of one or more the constituent helices in the structures. At present there is no standard easily accessible means for defining the orientation of a helix in a membrane protein structure. AnglerFish is a web-based tool for parameterising the angles of transmembrane helices based on PDB coordinates, with the helical orientations defined by the angles 'tilt' and 'swing'. AnglerFish is particularly useful for defining changes in structure between different states, including both symmetric and asymmetric transitions, and can be used to quantitate differences between related structures or different subunits within the same structure.","authors":[{"name":"Colledge M."},{"name":"Wallace B.A."}],"date":"2017-04-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"AnglerFish: A webserver for defining the geometry of \u03b1-helices in membrane proteins"},"pmcid":"PMC5860525","pmid":"28035031","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Protein structural motifs and surfaces","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0166"},{"term":"Protein structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2814"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"AnglerFish","home":"https://bio.tools/anglerfish","summary":"Method of determining the orientation of an \u03b1-helix relative to a defined axis in a rotationally symmetric protein structure such as a membrane protein channel.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:anglerfish/web/anglerfish.cryst.bbk.ac.uk","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":0,"citations":[],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btw781","pmcid":"PMC5860525","pmid":"28035031","ref_count":8,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1996"},{"count":1,"year":"2000"},{"count":1,"year":"2006"},{"count":1,"year":"2008"},{"count":1,"year":"2009"},{"count":1,"year":"2012"},{"count":1,"year":"2013"},{"count":1,"year":"2016"}],"title":"AnglerFish: a webserver for defining the geometry of \u03b1-helices in membrane proteins.","year":2017}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":false,"license":false,"operational":408,"redirects":[{"status":302,"url":"https://anglerfish.cryst.bbk.ac.uk/"}],"ssl":null,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"email":true}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/moni